id: 23
hanzi: 海鲜
pinyin: hǎi xiān
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: seafood; ocean delicacies; edible marine animals
  es: marisco; mariscos; frutos del mar; viandas marinas

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | edible fish, shellfish, crabs, and aquatic organisms caught from the sea | animales marinos comestibles (peces, mariscos, crustáceos) | 吃海鲜 (eat seafood)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 经过数星期的远洋航行，帆船停靠在热带小岛港湾，一家人品尝到了刚捕捞上来的鲜美海鲜。 | Jīngguò shù xīngqī de yuǎnyáng hángxíng, fānchuán tíngkào zài rèdài xiǎodǎo gǎngwān, yì jiā rén pǐncháng dào le gāng bǔlāo shànglái de xiānměi hǎixiān. | Following weeks of ocean cruising, the sailboat docked in a tropical lagoon, where the family relished succulent freshly caught seafood. | Tras semanas de singladura oceánica, el velero atracó en la bahía de una isla tropical, donde la familia degustó marisco fresco recién capturado.
  #2 | 沿海城市依托冷链物流与深海养殖基地，将优质活体海鲜在二十四小时内高效配送至内陆核心商圈。 | Yánhǎi chéngshì yītuō lěngliàn wùliú yǔ shēnhǎi yǎngzhí jīdì, jiāng yōuzhì huótǐ hǎixiān zài èrshísì xiǎoshí nèi gāoxiào pèisòng zhì nèilù héxīn shāngquān. | Coastal hubs leverage cold-chain logistics and mariculture farms to dispatch live seafood to inland commercial districts within 24 hours. | Las ciudades costeras aprovechan la cadena de frío y la acuicultura marina para suministrar marisco vivo a las urbes del interior en 24 horas.

